Uriel is a [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]] who has been on [[Geography/Ushas/index|Ushas]]. He looks like a middle-aged or older gentleman, with laugh lines and crow's feet, greying hair and an obviously hearty bearing. He is only ever met on boats, travelling, and he always plays a curious string instrument that is not native to the world he is on, such as a banjo.

On Ushas he crossed [[Phenomena/The Pale|the Pale]] untouched, saying only that it was mind over matter. He travelled a while with the party that would found [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]], let it be understood that he knew [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Mephistopheles|Mephistopheles]], and pointed them to [[Geography/Ushas/Sigil|Sigil]]. When they met him again he told them that the golden pin in the [[Geography/Ushas/Undermountain|Undermountain]] was a godslaying needle, the only one truly from Ushas's sphere, and wished them luck. He was a staunch ally.

On [[Geography/Althane/index|Althane]] [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]] met him on a boat going by the name Luce, and he taught them a resurrection ritual. A party on [[Geography/Færrin/index|Færrin]] saw him on a boat during the night of the [[Phenomena/Midnight Sun|Midnight Sun]], but did not speak with him.
